  "id": "Compound::DB00128 - Gene::445",
  "verbalization": "L-aspartic Acid is implicated in the interaction with Aspa, a protein that participates in the metabolic processes of aspartate. This interaction is further linked to Ass1, which is involved in the regulation of aspartate metabolism. The evidence suggests that L-aspartic Acid may influence Ass1 through its role in modulating aspartate metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which L-aspartic Acid could affect Ass1, possibly through direct or indirect interactions that alter metabolic activity. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, underscoring the importance of further experimental validation to confirm the precise nature of the interaction.",
